# Rename this file to seerr.txt. Only needed when Seerr is not on the same
# machine as Jellyfin: the app finds that case on its own.
#
# Two lines: the address of your request server, then its API key. Use the
# address and port you use to reach its web interface. http:// only, https://
# will not connect. If you leave the scheme off, http:// is assumed.
#
# The key is under Settings, General, API Key in the web interface. Anyone
# holding it can make requests as you, so treat the file as a password.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored.

http://192.168.1.10:5055
your-api-key-here
